    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MiniMax-AI/OpenAgentCore/tarball/v0.0.12-rc.1",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MiniMax-AI/OpenAgentCore/zipball/v0.0.12-rc.1",
    "body": "OpenAgentCore v0.0.12-rc.1\n\nPrerelease for testing in-place upgrades. `latest` still points to v0.0.11.\n\n**In-place upgrades.** An installation of v0.0.10 or later now upgrades in place and keeps its database, data volume, `.env`, secrets, Core key and installation ID. Back up first ([Upgrade](https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/OpenAgentCore/blob/main/docs/getting-started/operations.md#upgrade)), then run:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/OpenAgentCore/releases/download/v0.0.12-rc.1/install.sh | bash -s -- --version v0.0.12-rc.1 --upgrade --install-dir \"$HOME/.oac/core\"\n```\n\nThe installer checks the new release against the installation before it replaces any file, and initialization refuses downgrades. When you are ready, open **Settings** → **Sandbox and scheduling** and choose **Use this installation's Runtime** to move nodes to this release's Runtime.\n\n**Protocol changes:** none since v0.0.10. Nodes, the microsandbox helper, E2B templates and self-hosted machines keep working; applying this release's Runtime is optional.\n\nOther changes since v0.0.11:\n\n- A guided path from sign-in to a first Session, and failed Sessions that say what to do next.\n- Model provider rejections are classified, and Turns fail promptly when the model host is unreachable. Core errors appear in the console language.\n- A request log; settings reorganized, with platform settings and workspace storage in one place and idle suspension beside node capacity; health and capacity facts on their own pages.\n- Console tables and tabs fit on phones, and the console and docs use one set of terms.\n"
  },
